The measurement of activity concentration of natural radionuclides (226Ra, 232Th ad 40K) were done using a 50.8 mm × 50.8 mm Bicron NaI (Tl) gamma ray scintillation detector coupled to an Ortec 1024 channel DigiBase photomultiplier with 1024 digital multi-channel analyzer (MCA) and spectrum analysis software (Maestro). The detector has energy resolution of 9.1% at 662 keV gamma-ray line of 137Cs. The minimum detection limits of instrument for used energy lines of 40K, 226Ra and 232Th are 23.6 ± 2.6, 6.5 ± 2.8 and 2.4 ± 0.1 Bq/kg, respectively. Each sample was counted for 18,000 secs. The gamma ray spectrometer was calibrated (for both energy and efficiency) using the IAEA standards (RGU-1, RGTh-1 and RGK-1). The gamma ray energies used are 1764 keV, 2614 keV and 1460 keV for 226Ra, 232Th and 40K, respectively29. The activity concentration of the primordial radioactivity in the samples were calculated utilizing the formula\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
