For environmental impact assessment, the worldwide average values of eTh/eRa, eRa/eTh, eTh/K and eRa/K for safe environment are 3.50, 0.26, 0.067 and 0.067, respectively72,76. Therefore, from Table 10, the average values of eTh/eRa, eRa/K and eTh/K in all selected land uses were above the world averages of 3.50, 0.067, and 0.067, respectively, thus they are not safe radiologically based on the aforementioned trio ratios. However, the average values of eRa/eTh in ABT & DCS soils were greater than 0.26 while its values in other remaining land uses were < 0.26. This is suggestive of more non-radiologically safe state of ABT and DCS compared to other land uses investigated in this study. The average values of K/eTh ratio in soil samples from all land uses ranged between 0.014 (in W&FS) and 0.026 (in MVS) and fall below the threshold range (0.17%/ppm to 0.20%/ppm) of K/eTh content in underlying rock types that have not undergone alteration process77. The \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
